{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3142","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3142","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3142\",\"parent_revision\":\"6e8dcacc24f12a65a3cb2110aad1b63f2e4b0a2a579cdd90ad91a084301ff396\",\"root_revision\":\"6e8dcacc24f12a65a3cb2110aad1b63f2e4b0a2a579cdd90ad91a084301ff396\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nGoal: decide whether renaming the `implement-feature` skill to `delegate-implementation` is worth its cost as a prevention for the failure recorded in #3140.\\n\\nThe reasoning behind the proposal: an agent handed a skill named `implement-feature` and told to implement something reads the name as describing its own job. A name that says `delegate-implementation` makes the mismatch visible at the moment of reading, so the wrong actor sees that it is holding the wrong skill. The best prevention is the one where the right path is the only path visible to the actor.\\n\\nMeasured cost: 543 occurrences across 124 files. No plugin manifest declares the skill \u2014 it is discovered automatically \u2014 so there is no manifest edit, but every reference in skill bodies, reference workflows, agent files, docs, and generated artifacts moves. Roughly 53 of the hits are in historical research entries that record what was true when written and should probably not be rewritten. One generated workflow graph would need regeneration rather than editing.\\n\\nTwo findings that bear on the decision:\\n\\n- `dh:start-task` already occupies the do-the-implementation half of the proposed split. Creating a second skill for that role would duplicate it rather than separate two things that are currently fused.\\n- `dh:start-task`'s own frontmatter description names `implement-feature`, so that reference dangles on any rename and must move with it.\\n\\nPayoff and risk: the rename is a naming-only change with a large blast radius and no behavioural enforcement behind it. #3140 proposes removing hand-composed delegation prompts entirely, which closes the same path structurally. Deciding this item should follow, not precede, a decision on #3140 \u2014 if prompts are generated, the name carries much less weight.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the rename was requested directly; the cost measurement above was produced in response and the decision was left open.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **decide whether to rename implement-feature to delegate-implementation** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Proposed prevention for the #3060 over-orchestration incident\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"65c8258be7ef19c597885a98457b463f52d1ec52201ccc875d648a53f14df70e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQLLgUw\"}"}